# The build stage does `COPY . .`, so without this file `.env` — which holds the real
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY — is baked into an image layer and travels with every
# `fly deploy` / `docker push`. Deleting it in a later layer would not help: layers are additive
# and the secret stays readable in the earlier one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
dist
.git
.gitignore
.claude
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store

# Not needed to build or run, and they make the build context (and every rebuild) larger.
docs
test
README.md
CLAUDE.md
docker-compose.yml
